BiTSE 0.4

BiTSE 0.4 is the first BiTSe version that is released publicly.

This bundle contains the Bilingual grammar for Translation between
Swedish and English, BiTSE. The grammar is intended to be used with
systems that can run TDL-style grammars, such as the LKB (Copestake
2001), and can be used for parsing and generation.

For documentation see: 

 http://www.ida.liu.se/~sarst/bitse

The grammar is released under the LGPLLR, a version of the LGPL adapted to
linguistic resources. See LICENSE for details.

BiTSE is based on the LinGO Grammar Matrix (Matrix0.8). A copyright
notice for the Matrix can be found in matrix-licence.txt.



Architecture

BiTSE follows the standard LKB/Matrix (Matrix0.8) grammar set up as
concerns major file types; however, note that

- Type and lexicon files are to a large extent split between specific
for either Swedish or English, and shared between the languages.

- The rule files are not split between languages in the current (0.4)
version.


Test sentences

Test sentences and their parses can be found in the test/ catalogue.
Test files have the extension "txt"
The parsed versions have the extension "out"


Running BiTSE with LKB
The lkb catalogue contains configuration files et.c. for LKB.

To run BiTSE in LKB: start LKB and load the grammar via the
script file in the lkb catalogue.

BiTSE always runs with both Swedish and English loaded.

